{"id":2237,"age":68,"sex":"M","race":"Non-Hispanic White","insurance":"Medicare","profile":{"sex":"M","allergies":["NKDA"],"insurance":"Medicare","occupation":"Retired postal service supervisor","alcohol_use":"None","family_history":["Father: Myocardial infarction at age 58, deceased","Mother: Hypertension and hyperlipidemia, age 82","Brother: Coronary artery disease"],"race_ethnicity":"Non-Hispanic White","smoking_status":"Former smoker, 40 pack-years, quit 5 years ago","home_medications":[{"dose":"40 mg oral daily","name":"Furosemide"},{"dose":"20 mg oral daily","name":"Lisinopril"},{"dose":"12.5 mg oral twice daily","name":"Carvedilol"},{"dose":"40 mg oral daily","name":"Atorvastatin"},{"dose":"81 mg oral daily","name":"Aspirin"}],"surgical_history":["Percutaneous coronary intervention with drug-eluting stent (5 years prior)","Percutaneous coronary intervention (10 years prior)"],"chronic_conditions":["Coronary artery disease","Chronic systolic heart failure with reduced ejection fraction (LVEF 30%)","Hypertension","Hyperlipidemia","History of myocardial infarction"],"age_at_first_encounter":68},"comorbidities_listed":["Medication noncompliance","Old myocardial infarction","Hyperlipidemia","Essential hypertension","Heart failure with reduced ejection fraction"],"primary":{"did":1427,"code":"I20.0","name":"Acute coronary syndrome"},"filing":{"chapter":9,"block":"I20-I25","block_desc":"Ischemic heart diseases (I20-I25)"},"encounters":[{"id":9488,"date":"2020-01-15","type":"outpatient","dept":"Cardiology","attending":"Dr. Sarah Chen","cc":"Progressive substernal chest pressure radiating to the left arm over two months, now occurring at rest while reading the newspaper.","order":0,"method":"template","question_ids":[4471],"sections":[{"sid":29806,"type":"chief_complaint","lines":["Progressive substernal chest pressure radiating to the left arm over two months, now occurring at rest while reading the newspaper."]},{"sid":29807,"type":"hpi","lines":["He reports that for the past two months, he has experienced episodes of substernal pressure radiating to his left arm whenever he climbs stairs or walks briskly after meals.","Over the past week, the pain has become more frequent, sometimes occurring even while he reads his morning newspaper.","This chest discomfort is often accompanied by mild diaphoresis, shortness of breath, and a sense of impending doom.","He denies nausea, vomiting, or palpitations, but admits that he has been limiting his activity for fear of triggering the pain.","Despite these health issues, the patient maintains a very structured morning routine that he has followed for years.","He wakes at 6 a.m., prepares two slices of buttered toast and scrambled eggs, and enjoys a cup of strong black coffee.","He always spreads out the daily newspaper across his kitchen table and reads every section carefully, starting with international affairs before moving to local news and the arts.","After breakfast, he sometimes takes a short walk to a nearby cafe where he sits outside, sipping another coffee while watching passersby.","He takes great pleasure in photographing the small details of street life\u2014shadows cast by bicycles, the expressions of cafe patrons, and architectural patterns.","His passion is black-and-white photography, and he has built an extensive collection of prints over the years.","In recent months, however, his routine has been disrupted.","He has skipped his cafe visits because walking even two blocks provokes angina.","He also finds himself cutting breakfast short when chest pressure arises during reading.","His wife notes that he seems increasingly anxious and withdrawn, worried about the unpredictability of his symptoms.","Despite this, he has resisted coming to the doctor until now, believing he could manage on his own."]},{"sid":29808,"type":"pmh","lines":["Active Problem List:","- Coronary artery disease","- Chronic systolic heart failure with reduced ejection fraction (LVEF 30%)","- Hypertension","- Hyperlipidemia","- History of myocardial infarction","","The patient describes a long history of cardiovascular disease.","He was first diagnosed with hypertension 20 years ago, for which he has been intermittently compliant with medication.","Ten years ago, he was found to have hyperlipidemia, but he did not take his statin consistently due to concerns about muscle pain.","Five years ago, he suffered a myocardial infarction and underwent balloon angioplasty without stent placement.","Since then, he has been on aspirin but admits to occasionally forgetting his daily dose."]},{"sid":29809,"type":"psh","lines":["- Percutaneous coronary intervention with drug-eluting stent (5 years prior)","- Percutaneous coronary intervention (10 years prior)"]},{"sid":29810,"type":"medications","lines":["Home Medications:","- Furosemide 40 mg oral daily","- Lisinopril 20 mg oral daily","- Carvedilol 12.5 mg oral twice daily","- Atorvastatin 40 mg oral daily","- Aspirin 81 mg oral daily"]},{"sid":29811,"type":"allergies","lines":["NKDA"]},{"sid":29812,"type":"family_history","lines":["His father died of a heart attack at age 59, and his older brother had a coronary artery bypass at age 62."]},{"sid":29813,"type":"social_history","lines":["Smoking: Former smoker, 40 pack-years, quit 5 years ago.","Alcohol: None.","Occupation: Retired postal service supervisor."]},{"sid":29814,"type":"vitals","lines":["On examination, his blood pressure is 148/90 mm Hg, heart rate 84/min, and BMI 29."]},{"sid":29815,"type":"physical_exam","lines":["Cardiac auscultation reveals a normal S1 and S2 without murmurs, rubs, or gallops.","His lungs are clear, and there is no peripheral edema."]},{"sid":29816,"type":"imaging","lines":["Coronary angiography demonstrates multivessel coronary artery disease with a tight lesion in the left anterior descending artery."]},{"sid":29817,"type":"other_studies","lines":["An electrocardiogram shows nonspecific ST-T wave changes.","Stress testing is positive for inducible ischemia at low exertion,"]},{"sid":29818,"type":"plan","lines":["Given his unstable symptoms, the decision is made to proceed with percutaneous coronary intervention and stent placement.","In preparation for the procedure, he is started on aspirin and another drug that prevents platelet aggregation by blocking the glycoprotein IIb/IIIa receptor, thereby inhibiting platelet interaction with fibrinogen.","The patient is counseled about the increased risk of bleeding but agrees to therapy."]}],"orders":[{"order_id":847,"modality":"fluoroscopy","region":"chest","indication":"cp eval","provider":"Dr. Sarah Chen","priority":"urgent","datetime":"2020-01-15","result_sid":29816}]},{"id":9487,"date":"2020-04-15","type":"icu","dept":"Emergency Medicine","attending":"Dr. Marcus Johnson","cc":"Found collapsed at home after three days of progressive shortness of breath, orthopnea, and bilateral leg swelling.","order":1,"method":"hybrid","question_ids":[6118],"sections":[{"sid":29819,"type":"chief_complaint","lines":["Found collapsed at home after three days of progressive shortness of breath, orthopnea, and bilateral leg swelling."]},{"sid":29820,"type":"hpi","lines":["This patient returns three months after acute coronary syndrome evaluation.","His wife reports that over the past 3 days he has had progressive shortness of breath, orthopnea, and swelling in his legs."]},{"sid":29821,"type":"pmh","lines":["Active Problem List:","- Acute coronary syndrome (diagnosed 2020-01-15)","- Coronary artery disease","- Chronic systolic heart failure with reduced ejection fraction (LVEF 30%)","- Hypertension","- Hyperlipidemia","- History of myocardial infarction","","He has a history of coronary artery disease with a myocardial infarction 5 years ago, chronic systolic heart failure (LVEF 30%), hypertension, and hyperlipidemia."]},{"sid":29822,"type":"psh","lines":["- Percutaneous coronary intervention with drug-eluting stent (5 years prior)","- Percutaneous coronary intervention (10 years prior)"]},{"sid":29823,"type":"medications","lines":["His medications include furosemide, lisinopril, carvedilol, and atorvastatin, but he missed several doses recently due to nausea.","","Home Medications:","- Aspirin 81 mg oral daily"]},{"sid":29824,"type":"allergies","lines":["NKDA"]},{"sid":29825,"type":"family_history","lines":["- Father: Myocardial infarction at age 58, deceased","- Mother: Hypertension and hyperlipidemia, age 82","- Brother: Coronary artery disease"]},{"sid":29826,"type":"social_history","lines":["Smoking: Former smoker, 40 pack-years, quit 5 years ago.","Alcohol: None.","Occupation: Retired postal service supervisor."]},{"sid":29827,"type":"vitals","lines":["Blood pressure is 82/54 mm Hg, heart rate 112/min, respiratory rate 26/min, and oxygen saturation 88% on room air."]},{"sid":29828,"type":"physical_exam","lines":["On arrival, the patient appears diaphoretic and anxious.","Jugular venous distension is noted to the angle of the jaw at 45 degrees.","Cardiac auscultation reveals an S3 gallop; lung auscultation reveals bibasilar crackles.","Extremities are cool to the touch with delayed capillary refill, and pitting edema is present to the knees bilaterally."]},{"sid":29829,"type":"labs","lines":["Laboratory studies reveal elevated BNP and mildly elevated troponin."]},{"sid":29830,"type":"imaging","lines":["An urgent chest x-ray reveals the following."]},{"sid":29831,"type":"other_studies","lines":["ECG shows sinus tachycardia with nonspecific ST-T changes."]},{"sid":29832,"type":"plan","lines":["The patient is placed on supplemental oxygen and undergoes right heart catheterization for further hemodynamic assessment."]}],"orders":[{"order_id":848,"modality":"xray","region":"chest","indication":"SOB","provider":"Dr. Marcus Johnson","priority":"stat","datetime":"2020-04-15","result_sid":29830}]},{"id":9489,"date":"2021-01-15","type":"icu","dept":"Emergency Medicine","attending":"Dr. Priya Patel","cc":"Sudden onset of severe shortness of